      "RWR",
      "[Expert R1] (Detect atomicity violations in the code.)\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"g1\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Read\"],\n            \"lines\": [29, 10, 31]\n        },\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"g1\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Read\"],\n            \"lines\": [29, 14, 31]\n        },\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"g1\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Read\"],\n            \"lines\": [31, 10, 35]\n        },\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"g1\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Read\"],\n            \"lines\": [31, 14, 35]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n[System] Expert first round completed in 8.14 seconds\n\n[Judge R1] (Validate the expert's defect report and check control/interrupt conditions.)\nLet me analyze each read/write operation for the global variable `g1` to determine if the reported atomicity violations are valid.\n\n## Step 1: Check Control Conditions\n\nFor each read/write operation:\n\n1. **Line 9 (Read g1)**: `int tmp1 = g1 + 1;`\n   - This is in `svp_simple_614_001_isr_1` which is an interrupt handler\n   - No control conditions guard this operation - it will execute whenever the interrupt occurs\n\n2. **Line 10 (Write g1)**: `g1 = tmp1;`\n   - Same as above - no control conditions, executes when interrupt occurs\n\n3. **Line 13 (Read g1)**: `int tmp2 = g1 - 1;`\n   - No control conditions, executes when interrupt occurs\n\n4. **Line 14 (Write g1)**: `g1 = tmp2;`\n   - No control conditions, executes when interrupt occurs\n\n5. **Line 29 (Read g1)**: `__VERIFIER_assert(g1 == 0);`\n   - This is in `svp_simple_614_001_main`\n   - No control conditions guard this operation - it will execute when main runs\n\n6. **Line 31 (Read g1)**: `__VERIFIER_assert(g1 == 0);`\n   - Same as above - no control conditions\n\n7. **Line 35 (Read g1)**: `__VERIFIER_assert(g1 == 0);`\n   - Same as above - no control conditions\n\n## Step 2: Check Interrupt Status\n\nLooking at the code:\n- There are no `disable_isr()` or `enable_isr()` calls in the entire program\n- The interrupt handler `svp_simple_614_001_isr_1` is not explicitly enabled or disabled\n- By default, interrupts are enabled, so the ISR can preempt the main function\n\n## Step 3: Variable Value Analysis\n\n- `g1` is a global variable initialized to 0 (implicit initialization in C)\n- The ISR modifies `g1` through the sequence: read → add 1 → write → read → subtract 1 → write\n- This sequence effectively leaves `g1` unchanged (g1 = (g1 + 1) - 1 = g1)\n- However, between the write at line 10 and write at line 14, `g1` has the value `g1_initial + 1`\n\n## Step 4: Accessibility Analysis\n\nAll read/write operations can be executed:\n- The ISR can preempt the main function at any point\n- All operations in both main and ISR are unconditionally executed\n- No interrupt disabling occurs to prevent ISR execution\n\n## Summary of Analysis\n\nAll reported atomicity violations are valid because:\n1. All read/write operations can be executed\n2. The ISR can preempt the main function at any time\n3. The operations in the ISR are not atomic with respect to the main function\n\nThe violations represent scenarios where:\n- Main reads `g1` (lines 29, 31, 35)\n- ISR writes to `g1` (lines 10, 14)\n- Main reads `g1` again\n\nThese are legitimate atomicity violations.\n\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"g1\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Read\"],\n            \"lines\": [29, 10, 31]\n        },\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"g1\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Read\"],\n            \"lines\": [29, 14, 31]\n        },\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"g1\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Read\"],\n            \"lines\": [31, 10, 35]\n        },\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"g1\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Read\"],\n            \"lines\": [31, 14, 35]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n[Expert R2] (Refine the report based on judge feedback, re-check for missed or false defects.)\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"g1\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Read\"],\n            \"lines\": [29, 10, 31]\n        },\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"g1\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Read\"],\n            \"lines\": [29, 14, 31]\n        },\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"g1\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Read\"],\n            \"lines\": [31, 10, 35]\n        },\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"g1\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Read\"],\n            \"lines\": [31, 14, 35]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n"
